/E (In 2024, ByteDance introduced Hyper-Connections \(HC\), an enhancement to the standard residual connection architecture that has powered neural networks since 2016.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (The idea was elegant: instead of a single information pathway through the model \(think of it as a one-lane highway\), create multiple parallel streams \(a multi-lane superhighway\). The performance gains were immediate and substantial.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Models using HC showed 2-5% improvements across benchmarks, particularly on complex reasoning tasks. Teams got excited. Papers were published. Implementation began.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
